# Alih ships archives whose integrity is proven by checksums over exact bytes.
# Git's end-of-line conversion rewrites those bytes on checkout, which on
# Windows made every fixture disagree with the manifest that seals it: each file
# grew by one byte per line, and the frozen v0.2.4 compatibility corpus stopped
# being frozen. Test evidence must reach every platform exactly as recorded.
**/testdata/** -text

# The archive database is binary; never diff or convert it.
*.db binary

# Shell scripts must keep LF wherever they are checked out, because the
# installer is executed on POSIX systems and published as a release asset.
*.sh text eol=lf
